Relevant columns and their potential usage

• countries.country_name: identify France  
• countries.country_id: join to customers.country_id  
• customers.cust_id: join to sales.cust_id  
• customers.country_id: links each customer to a country  
• sales.amount_sold: the sales figure we will aggregate  
• sales.time_id: join to times to obtain year / month  
• sales.channel_id: join to channels so we can keep only rows where channel_total_id = 1  
• sales.promo_id: join to promotions so we can keep only rows where promo_total_id = 1  
• times.calendar_year, times.calendar_month_number: needed to pick 2019 / 2020 and to build 2021 projection  
• channels.channel_total_id: must be 1 for the filter  
• promotions.promo_total_id: must be 1 for the filter  
• currency.country, currency.year, currency.month, currency.to_us: FX rate to translate local sales into USD  

Typical conditions that will be used

• countries.country_name = 'France'  
• channels.channel_total_id = 1  
• promotions.promo_total_id = 1  
• times.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)         -- to derive growth rate  
• times.calendar_year = 2021                   -- when projecting  
• currency.country = countries.country_name  
• currency.year  = times.calendar_year  
• currency.month = times.calendar_month_number  

Exploratory SQL statements  
(they gradually go from very simple look‑ups to complex joins; all use DISTINCT where it makes sense and each one is limited to 20 rows)

```sql
-- 1. List a few country names to confirm France exists
SELECT DISTINCT country_name
FROM countries
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check the “channel_total_id” values which should contain the value 1
SELECT DISTINCT channel_total_id
FROM channels
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Check the “promo_total_id” values which should contain the value 1
SELECT DISTINCT promo_total_id
FROM promotions
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Grab raw sales rows already restricted to promo_total_id = 1 and channel_total_id = 1
SELECT s.*
FROM   sales AS s
JOIN   channels   AS c ON c.channel_id = s.channel_id
JOIN   promotions AS p ON p.promo_id   = s.promo_id
WHERE  c.channel_total_id = 1
  AND  p.promo_total_id   = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect the years available in the times table
SELECT DISTINCT calendar_year
FROM times
ORDER BY calendar_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. See monthly sales (any country) for 2019 to ensure data volume
SELECT t.calendar_year,
       t.calendar_month_number,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_sales
FROM   sales AS s
JOIN   times AS t ON t.time_id = s.time_id
WHERE  t.calendar_year = 2019
GROUP  BY t.calendar_year, t.calendar_month_number
ORDER  BY t.calendar_month_number
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate 2019 monthly sales *just for France* and already filtered by promo / channel
SELECT t.calendar_month_number,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) AS fr_2019_sales
FROM   sales AS s
JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id     = s.time_id
JOIN   customers  AS cu ON cu.cust_id    = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = cu.country_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id
JOIN   promotions AS pr ON pr.promo_id   = s.promo_id
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  t.calendar_year      = 2019
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  pr.promo_total_id    = 1
GROUP  BY t.calendar_month_number
ORDER  BY t.calendar_month_number
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same aggregation for 2020 so we can derive the growth rate
SELECT t.calendar_month_number,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) AS fr_2020_sales
FROM   sales AS s
JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id     = s.time_id
JOIN   customers  AS cu ON cu.cust_id    = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = cu.country_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id
JOIN   promotions AS pr ON pr.promo_id   = s.promo_id
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  t.calendar_year      = 2020
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  pr.promo_total_id    = 1
GROUP  BY t.calendar_month_number
ORDER  BY t.calendar_month_number
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Convert France 2019 monthly sales into USD using the currency table
SELECT t.calendar_month_number,
       SUM(s.amount_sold) / MAX(cur.to_us) AS fr_2019_sales_usd
FROM   sales AS s
JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id     = s.time_id
JOIN   customers  AS cu ON cu.cust_id    = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = cu.country_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id
JOIN   promotions AS pr ON pr.promo_id   = s.promo_id
JOIN   currency   AS cur
       ON  cur.country = co.country_name
       AND cur.year    = t.calendar_year
       AND cur.month   = t.calendar_month_number
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  t.calendar_year      = 2019
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  pr.promo_total_id    = 1
GROUP  BY t.calendar_month_number
ORDER  BY t.calendar_month_number
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. One‑shot query that puts everything together:
--     1) 2019 & 2020 monthly USD sales for France
--     2) derive monthly growth rate
--     3) apply growth to project 2021 monthly sales
--     4) take the average (mean) of each 2021 month
--     5) compute the median of those 12 averages
WITH fr_2019 AS (
    SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS mth,
           SUM(s.amount_sold) / MAX(cur.to_us) AS usd_sales_2019
    FROM   sales AS s
    JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id     = s.time_id
    JOIN   customers  AS cu ON cu.cust_id    = s.cust_id
    JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = cu.country_id
    JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id
    JOIN   promotions AS pr ON pr.promo_id   = s.promo_id
    JOIN   currency   AS cur
           ON  cur.country = co.country_name
           AND cur.year    = 2019
           AND cur.month   = t.calendar_month_number
    WHERE  co.country_name     = 'France'
      AND  t.calendar_year     = 2019
      AND  ch.channel_total_id = 1
      AND  pr.promo_total_id   = 1
    GROUP  BY t.calendar_month_number
), fr_2020 AS (
    SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS mth,
           SUM(s.amount_sold) / MAX(cur.to_us) AS usd_sales_2020
    FROM   sales AS s
    JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id     = s.time_id
    JOIN   customers  AS cu ON cu.cust_id    = s.cust_id
    JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = cu.country_id
    JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id
    JOIN   promotions AS pr ON pr.promo_id   = s.promo_id
    JOIN   currency   AS cur
           ON  cur.country = co.country_name
           AND cur.year    = 2020
           AND cur.month   = t.calendar_month_number
    WHERE  co.country_name     = 'France'
      AND  t.calendar_year     = 2020
      AND  ch.channel_total_id = 1
      AND  pr.promo_total_id   = 1
    GROUP  BY t.calendar_month_number
), growth AS (
    SELECT a.mth,
           (b.usd_sales_2020 - a.usd_sales_2019) / NULLIF(a.usd_sales_2019,0) AS growth_rate
    FROM   fr_2019 AS a
    JOIN   fr_2020 AS b ON b.mth = a.mth
), proj_2021 AS (
    SELECT g.mth,
           (1 + g.growth_rate) * b.usd_sales_2020 AS projected_2021_usd
    FROM   growth AS g
    JOIN   fr_2020 AS b ON b.mth = g.mth
), month_avg AS (
    SELECT mth,
           projected_2021_usd AS avg_monthly_2021_usd
    FROM   proj_2021
), ordered AS (
    SELECT avg_monthly_2021_usd,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY avg_monthly_2021_usd) AS rn,
           COUNT(*)     OVER ()                                 AS cnt
    FROM   month_avg
)
SELECT AVG(avg_monthly_2021_usd) AS median_2021_avg_monthly_usd
FROM   ordered
WHERE  rn IN ((cnt + 1)/2, (cnt + 2)/2);   -- works for both even & odd counts
```

Each query above is limited to a maximum of 20 result rows (except the final one which produces a single value).
